elcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "contents": [{"value": {"coverimg": "enpe7n3le02ob09re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"time": "0", "text": "<strong>Carol: </strong> Hi, are you ready for today's exam?</br>\n<strong>Daniel: </strong> I don't feel ready, but I must pass it! </br><strong>Carol: </strong> I could be the one who helps you. We have to study a lot! Let's review a key term first, what's a data type? </br><strong>Daniel: </strong> Well, it's a classification that programmers do according to the use they want to give to the data. A type can define the meaning, the usage, and the processes for storing the different values within a piece of data.", "image": "enpe7n3le02ob09re2img01.jpg", "id": 0}, {"time": "30000", "text": "<strong>Carol: </strong> See? You're clever, you're a bookworm! Now, what's a structured data type? </br>\n<strong>Daniel: </strong> I've been studying eagerly. Structured data types are common in modern computer languages. You know that the data types that we've studied so far can take just one value, right? Unlike those, structured data types can take more than a piece of data. </br>\n<strong>Carol: </strong> Now I remember. The array is a basic structured data type. </br>\n<strong>Daniel: </strong> That one can hold a collection of variables or values. </br>\n<strong>Carol: </strong> We can say then that structured data types help define complex data structures. Do you have another example? </br>\n<strong>Daniel: </strong> Remember the programming language called Pascal? There you can find a structured data type known as record.", "image": "enpe7n3le02ob09re2img02.jpg", "id": 1}, {"time": "82000", "text": "<strong>Carol: </strong> That one is used for collecting different data types that define a single value. For example, if you want to define a pillow, it'll give information on the size, the fabric, and the color. </br>\n<strong>Daniel: </strong> That one is a good example. The teacher told us that when using Pascal, we needed to write the code carefully because the ones who are new in this programming language tend to forget the end keyword. Can you give me more examples of structured data types?   </br>\n<strong>Carol: </strong>The Boolean data type and the Struct in C programming, which is a composite data type .</br>\n<strong>Daniel: </strong> Good! I think we're ready! I would feel like a million dollars if I pass the exam!", "image": "enpe7n3le02ob09re2img03.jpg", "id": 2}], "audiosrc": "enpe7n3le02ob09re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "title": "", "id": 1, "type": "audio"}], "id": 0, "type": "scholar"}]}